\f1\b\fs28 \ul Work Ethics:
\f0\b0\fs22 \ulnone \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The RACI Framework is a project management tool used to map out and clarify team roles, task ownership, and responsibilities. The acronym stands for Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, and Informed. \
The RACI framework categorizes team involvement into four roles:\
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Responsible (R): The "doers". These individuals or teams handle the actual work, execution, and task completion.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Accountable (A): The owner. This single person is ultimately answerable for the success or failure of the task and holds the final sign-off authority. Every task must have exactly one accountable person.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Consulted (C): Subject-matter experts or stakeholders whose opinions are sought before work is finalized. Communication is two-way.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Informed (I): People who need to be kept up-to-date on project progress or results, but are not directly involved in the work or decision-making. Communication is one-way.\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 \cb3 Powerful Prompt Phrases:
\f0\b0\fs22 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Here are some examples of powerful prompt phrases:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Give AI a process to follow\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Think step-by-step.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
First, [action 1]. Second, [action 2]. Finally, [action 3].\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Define the audience and tone\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Write this for an audience of [audience type, e.g., executives].\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The tone should be [tone, e.g., professional].\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Set hard constraints\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Write a one paragraph summary.\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Focus exclusively on [topic A, e.g. revenue] and do not mention [topic B, e.g., costs].\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Request a critique\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Critique this text from the perspective of a [role, e.g., potential customer].\
\ls9\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Play devil's advocate. What is the strongest counterargument to this?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Generate alternatives\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Give me 3 different versions of this.\
\ls10\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
What's an alternative approach to solving this problem?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Deepen or expand on the initial output\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Elaborate on point 2.\
\ls11\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Provide more detail and specific examples for the section about [section].\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 \cb3 \ul \ulc2 Generate visuals with AI
\f0\b0\fs22 \ulnone \
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 What is multimodality?\
To break it down, modalities are different types of formats, like text, image, or audio.\'a0\
Multimodality is useful because it allows you to give Gemini more detailed and richer context when prompting it. Instead of telling it what you want using only words, you can enrich your instructions with images, video, and audio.\'a0\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 \ul Understand how AI agents work
\f0\b0\fs22 \ulnone \
An AI agent operates using three core components:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Models: Models are computer programs trained on vast amounts of data, which allows them to recognize patterns. When you give an AI agent a goal, the model uses its training to predict which tasks are necessary to achieve that goal and how to use the tools available to complete it.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls12\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Permissions: AI agents connect to other software and tools through specific permissions you grant. These settings act as guardrails, controlling how the agent executes tasks within the parameters you set. For example, if you assign an agent to manage your inbox, you can restrict its access to only read unread messages.\cb1 \
\ls12\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Goals: A goal is the broad objective you provide an AI agent, such as "Organize the Q3 kickoff meeting.\'94 Once a goal is set, the agent operates in a continuous loop until the goal is complete.\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl1\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Analyze: The agent uses its model to determine the necessary first task, like connecting with your calendar to find free time\'a0\cb1 \
\ls12\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Act: Once permissions are granted, the agent executes that task, like finding a time for the team to connect\cb1 \
\ls12\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Observe: The agent reviews the result of its action and ensures it's aligned with the goal, like checking the selected time to make sure everyone is available\'a0\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
